# Changelog

All notable changes to the **Marine Eco System** project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/),  
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

---

## [1.0.0] - 2026-09-17

### Added
- Initial release of the Marine Eco System website
- **Home Page** (`index.html`) with project overview and featured marine initiatives
- **About Page** with History, Mission Statement, and Vision Statement
- **Services Page** showcasing:
  - Coastal & Beach Cleanups
  - Wildlife Rehabilitation Support
  - Community Education & Outreach
- **Enquiry Page** with detailed form for:
  - Volunteer Sign-up
  - General Enquiries
  - Donations & Sponsorships
  - Guided Marine Tours
- **Contact Us Page** including:
  - Postal and physical address
  - Opening hours
  - Google Maps embed (Summerstrand, Gqeberha)
  - Contact form
- Shared header navigation across all pages
- Multi-column responsive footer with:
  - Conservation links
  - Get Involved section
  - About the Trust links
  - Contact details and social media icons
  - Newsletter subscription form
- Responsive CSS using Flexbox and CSS Grid
- CSS Variables for consistent colour theming
- Logo integration in the site header
- Mobile-friendly breakpoints for tablets and phones

### Technical
- Pure HTML5 and CSS3 (no JavaScript frameworks)
- Semantic HTML structure
- Accessible navigation with ARIA labels
- SVG social media icons (Facebook, Instagram, WhatsApp)

---

## Future Planned Updates

### Planned
- Form validation and backend integration for enquiry and contact forms
- Image optimisation and additional project photo galleries
- Dark mode / high-contrast theme option
- Blog / Conservation News section
- Multi-language support (English / isiXhosa)

---

